%N A399482 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^(k+1) * O(k)^2/k, where O(k) = A350669(k)/A350670(k) is the k-th odd harmonic number (or harmonic number of the second kind).
%H A399482 Anthony Sofo and Amrik Singh Nimbran, <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/math7090833">Euler sums and integral connections</a>, Mathematics, Vol. 7, No. 9 (2019), Article 833. See p. 9, eq. (21).
%H A399482 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-02462-8">(Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer International Publishing, 2019, section 3.20, pp. 127-131, eq. (3.115).
%H A399482 Yifan Yang, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmaa.2008.01.094">Apéry limits and special values of L-functions</a>, Journal of Mathematical Analysis and Applications, Vol. 343, No. 1 (2008), pp. 492-513. See Theorem 5, p. 510.
%H A399482 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A399482 Equals 7*zeta(3)/16 (Sofo and Nimbran, 2019).
%F A399482 Equals A233091/2 = A399216/4.
%F A399482 Equals -Integral_{x=0..1} arctan(x) * log((1-x)/(1+x)) / (1+x^2) dx (Vălean, 2019).
%F A399482 Equals Sum_{k>=2, k even} (k^3 + k^5)/(k^2 - 1)^4 (see _Peter Bala_'s Dec 04 2013 formula in A002117).
%F A399482 Equals -Integral_{x=0..Pi/2} x*log(2*cos(x)) dx (see _Jean-François Alcover_'s Apr 02 2013 formula in A002117).
